Employee Sentiment Analysis

This project performs automated sentiment analysis on employee emails/messages and generates insights such as sentiment trends, monthly scores, employee rankings, flight risk identification, and predictive modeling.

Project Overview

The main objectives of the project are:

Sentiment Labeling – Automatically classify each message as Positive, Negative, or Neutral using a pretrained transformer model.

Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) – Analyze message patterns and visualize trends over time.

Employee Score Calculation – Compute monthly sentiment scores for each employee.

Employee Ranking – Identify top positive and negative employees per month.

Flight Risk Identification – Flag employees at risk of leaving based on negative message frequency.

Predictive Modeling – Use linear regression to model sentiment trends and predict employee monthly sentiment scores.

Requirements

Python 3.9+

Libraries:

pip install pandas numpy matplotlib seaborn transformers scikit-learn openpyxl tqdm


Input dataset: CSV or Excel file with columns:

Subject, body, date, from

How to Run

Set the input file path and output folder in the script:

input_path = '/content/drive/MyDrive/test.xlsx'  # or .csv
output_folder = '/content/drive/MyDrive/sentiment_project_outputs'


Run the script. It will automatically:

Label sentiment of messages

Perform EDA and save charts

Compute monthly employee sentiment scores

Rank employees

Identify flight risk employees

Train and evaluate a linear regression model

Save all outputs to the output_folder

Outputs

All outputs are saved to the output_folder. Key files include:

Labeled Dataset

test_labeled.csv / test_labeled.xlsx – Original dataset augmented with sentiment labels and numeric scores.

EDA Outputs

sentiment_distribution.png – Bar chart of overall sentiment distribution.

monthly_sentiment_trends.png – Stacked bar chart of monthly sentiment counts.

monthly_sentiment_counts.csv – CSV summary of monthly sentiment counts.

Separate monthly sentiment charts:

positive_trend.png

negative_trend.png

neutral_trend.png

Employee Scores & Rankings

employee_monthly_scores.csv – Monthly sentiment scores per employee.

top_3_positive_per_month.csv – Top 3 positive employees per month.

top_3_negative_per_month.csv – Top 3 negative employees per month.

Flight Risk

flight_risk_employees.csv – Employees identified as flight risk based on rolling 30-day negative email count.

Predictive Modeling (Linear Regression)

regression_predictions.csv – Actual vs predicted monthly sentiment scores.

regression_coefficients.csv – Coefficients of features in the linear regression model.

Features Used for Predictive Modeling

For each employee per month:

msg_count – Total messages sent

avg_message_length – Average message length (characters)

avg_word_count – Average word count per message

pct_negative – Proportion of messages classified as negative

pct_positive – Proportion of messages classified as positive

Target: monthly_score (sum of message scores)

Notes

Sentiment labeling uses DistilBERT fine-tuned on SST-2.

Messages with unparseable dates or missing body/from are excluded.

Flight risk considers a rolling 30-day window, not just calendar months.

Monthly sentiment trends are visualized in separate charts for Positive, Negative, and Neutral messages.

